<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n393" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ac-crēdo</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">adc.</span></b> ), dĭdi, dĭtum,
		3, v. a. (<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>pres. sub.</i> adcredŭas,
					<i><span class="en">Plaut. Asin. 5, 2, 4</span></i>), <i>to yield one's belief to</i> another, i. e. <i>to believe unconditionally</i> (rare).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(a).</b> With <i>dat.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quisnam istuc adcredat tibi?</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Asin. 3, 3, 37</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">neque mi posthac quidquam adcreduas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 5, 2, 4</span></i>
			; so, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tibi nos,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor. Ep. 1, 15, 25</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(b).</b>
			<i>Aliquid</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">facile hoc,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lucr.
					3, 856</span></i>
			. 
			 —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(g).</b>
			<b>
				<i>Absol.</i>
			</b>: vix adcredens, * <i><span class="en">Cic. Att. 6,
				2, 3</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">primo non accredidit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Nep. Dat.
					3</span></i>
			. 4.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
